# Rust conventions

- Keep modules private in `src/lib.rs` and re-export the public surface explicitly.
- Constructors wrapping raw `MIDIObjectRef` / endpoint refs should stay `pub(crate)` unless exposing them is intentional API.
- Map CoreMIDI failures with the existing `result_from_status` / `unit_result_from_status` helpers; use `Option` for absent objects.
- Put unit tests in the same file under `#[cfg(test)]`.
- When touching packet/event layout or callbacks, preserve alignment, timestamp ordering, and Core Foundation retain/get rules already used nearby.
- Link Apple CoreMIDI docs in public item docs the same way neighboring APIs do.
